    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44818" root="&#xA;                        يمن&#xA;                    " body-key="Y1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَنُ</span></b> 
                         [The <i>right, as opposed to</i> the <i>left;</i> see Kur,
xix. 53, xx. 82, and xxviii. 30:] <i>contr. of</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْسَرُ</span>;
and [in like manner] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيْمَنَةٌ</span></b>  is <i>contr. of</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَيْسَرَةٌ</span>.
(S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْمَنُ</span>, <i>contr. of</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْأَمُ</span>, as signifying The
<i>right,</i> opposed to the <i>left:</i> and as signifying
<i>Lucky,</i> or <i>auspicious:</i> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيَامِنُ</span>. See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْأَمُ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
It is also used in the sense of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُمْنٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْأَمُ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
Also <i>More,</i> and <i>most, lucky,</i> or <i>auspicious,</i> or
<i>happy:</i> see 8 in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فئل</span>.

